  "page": 341,
  "line": 25,
  "situation": "The four cells of the unction print their own references: compunction, Acts ii. 37, *pricked in their heart*; clear knowledge, 2 Cor. ii. 6 as printed; fervent prayer, Jas. v. 16; love shed abroad, Rom. v. 5. Three take their noun from the Vulgate of their own verse — *compunctio* from *compuncti sunt corde*, *diffusio charitatis* from *caritas Dei diffusa est* — which is what convicts the fourth. 2 Cor. ii. 6 concerns a man punished by the many and has nothing to do with knowledge; 2 Cor. iv. 6 reads *ad illuminationem scientiæ claritatis Dei* and supplies *scientia* exactly as the others are supplied. A single wrong numeral, ii for iv. Kept as printed; the true verse is 2 Cor. iv. 6 — the quarrying habit of the facing leaf doing forensic work one page later.",
  "source": "identified",
  "band": "R",
  "numbering": true,
  "plateFigure": true
 },
